{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <stack>\n#include <utility>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\nll n;\nint sol = 1e9;\n\nstruct State {\n    ll val;\n    int cost;\n};\n\nvoid dfs(ll start, int startCost) {\n    stack<State> st;\n    st.push({start, startCost});\n    while (!st.empty()) {\n        State cur = st.top(); st.pop();\n        ll v = cur.val;\n        int c = cur.cost;\n        if (c >= sol) continue;\n        if (v == 0) {\n            sol = c;\n            continue;\n        }\n        ll s = 1;\n        int digits = 1;\n        while (s * 10 + 1 <= v) {\n            s = s * 10 + 1;\n            digits++;\n        }\n        // push second branch first so that first branch is processed first\n        st.push({s * 10 + 1 - v, c + digits + 1});\n        st.push({v % s, c + digits * (v / s)});\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n;\n    dfs(n, 0);\n    cout << sol;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.util.Stack;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static long n;\n    static int sol = 1000000000;\n\n    static class State {\n        long val;\n        int cost;\n        State(long val, int cost) {\n            this.val = val;\n            this.cost = cost;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void dfs(long start, int startCost) {\n        Stack<State> st = new Stack<>();\n        st.push(new State(start, startCost));\n        while (!st.isEmpty()) {\n            State cur = st.pop();\n            long v = cur.val;\n            int c = cur.cost;\n            if (c >= sol) continue;\n            if (v == 0) {\n                sol = c;\n                continue;\n            }\n            long s = 1;\n            int digits = 1;\n            while (s * 10 + 1 <= v) {\n                s = s * 10 + 1;\n                digits++;\n            }\n            // push second branch first so that first branch is processed first\n            st.push(new State(s * 10 + 1 - v, c + digits + 1));\n            st.push(new State(v % s, c + digits * (int)(v / s)));\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextLong();\n        dfs(n, 0);\n        System.out.println(sol);\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.99\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00014423283573705703, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.2291887944447808e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.10032951831817627, -6.794906312279636e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -7.545663538621739e-05, -0.0002619877050165087, 0.0, -0.02282571606338024, -0.005235651042312384, -0.0011767374817281961, -0.039186518639326096, -0.3581503927707672, -0.00033623288618400693, -6.198863957251888e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.9682672902708873e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.011055760085582733, -0.011049157939851284, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.57627811808924